TASK-209 runtime harness: the command palette's rows per profile. Temporary
code, never committed to Detour/. Gated on DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR;
DETOUR_VERIFY_APPEARANCE light or dark; DETOUR_VERIFY_FIXTURE a loopback
server (python3 -I -m http.server 8939 --bind 127.0.0.1 over a dir with
shared.html titled "Shared board" and acme-board.html titled "Acme board").
Data dir DetourVerify2090. Fixture: the Default profile (Home, Errands, its
Quick Detour scope) and a "Work 209" profile (Acme), overlapping URLs and
titles seeded through HistoryDatabase.recordVisit (mail.example: "Family
mail" in Home, "Acme mail - Inbox (3)" in Acme, recorded last so the shared
title is Work's; docs.example/plan: "Holiday plan" in Errands, "Acme launch
plan" in Acme; news.example and a Quick Detour recipes.example only in
Default; wiki.acme.example only in Work), and open tabs at the same URL in
Errands and Acme. A window per profile; each palette entry point (Cmd+T,
Cmd+L, the faux address bar, the Quick Detour launcher on each profile, a
Private window) is opened, a query typed, and every row of the palette's
table logged with a LEAK flag for a row carrying the other profile's marker.
Step 07b (code review): a palette left open while the window switches to an
empty space of the other profile. run.sh is TASK-213's (SHOOT lines served
with screencapture -l, only the launched PID killed). When Detour cannot be
made frontmost (a locked screen), palettes are opened by direct calls
(newTab, focusAddressBar, openCommandPaletteInPlace) and text is typed
through the field editor's insertText, one character at a time.

    git apply docs/harness/task209-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    run.sh light; run.sh dark
    git apply -R docs/harness/task209-harness.patch && xcodegen generate

Results (2026-10-27, light and dark, screen locked: direct calls and the
field editor, no pixels captured): 0 leaks in 18 palettes per run. Default
window: "mail" completes to mail.example labelled "Family mail" (the shared
title is Work's), "plan" finds "Holiday plan" from the Errands space (another
space of the profile, new), "lentil" finds the Quick Detour visit (new),
"acme" finds nothing from history, "board" offers one Switch to Tab ("Shared
board" in Errands) and not Work's two. Work window: only Acme rows; "family"
and "lentil" find nothing; the faux bar's palette the same. Launcher: Work
"plan" gives "Acme launch plan", Default "lentil" the recipe; filler rows
from each profile only. Private window: no history row and no tab (search
suggestions only). 07b: after the switch the open palette lists Work's tabs
and history, before it Default's.

